{"title":"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(coord_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(coord bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_-_Law_of_Cosines_and_Double_Angle_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 - Law of Cosines and Double Angle Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_-_Complex_Number_and_Double_Angle_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 - Complex Number and Double Angle Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cyrus the frog jumps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units in a direction, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more in another direction. What is the probability that he lands less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit away from his starting position?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38dd0fdea2a93aab134fdef06ece2eadd5b39a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~\\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~\\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~\\frac{\\arctan \\frac{1}{2}}{\\pi}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~\\frac{2\\arcsin \\frac{1}{4}}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"504\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023AMC12BP20.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f4/2023AMC12BP20.png/500px-2023AMC12BP20.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"336\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f4/2023AMC12BP20.png/750px-2023AMC12BP20.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f4/2023AMC12BP20.png/1000px-2023AMC12BP20.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let Cyrus's starting position be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. WLOG, let the place Cyrus lands at for his first jump be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, Cyrus can reach all the points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that Cyrus will land less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6a430c21adfa363071034a2a23e0197d66f2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4 \\alpha }{ 2 \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9cfcc2453f1364d19d584a748bcb20a1ae4f004.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\alpha = \\frac{ \\frac12 }{2} = \\frac14, \\quad \\alpha = \\arcsin \\frac14\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f31034de76a6ae51c2ee32e928e18e2bba70d95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4 \\arcsin \\frac14 }{ 2 \\pi} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2 \\arcsin \\frac{1}{4}}{\\pi}}\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> the position after the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th jump.\nThus, to fall into the region centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and with radius 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d74825bd9ed39558ceeea659af4b904b6ad0271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A_2 A_1 A_0 &lt; 2 \\arcsin \\frac{1/2}{2} = 2 \\arcsin \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"294\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edb5c671433291b14a0e16f099947181f8a4717.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{2 \\cdot 2 \\arcsin \\frac{1}{4}}{2 \\pi} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2 \\arcsin \\frac{1}{4}}{\\pi}}. \\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28coord_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(coord_bash)\">Solution 3(coord bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(coord bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the orgin be the starting point of frog. Then, WLOG assume that after the first jump, it is at the point (2,0). Then, the range of all possible places the frog can jump to at its second jump is the circle with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b7bd588dade0077e6ae1a9be7c4b7d55b9b30a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)^2+y^2=2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />.If it landed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit within its starting point (the orgin), then it is inside the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dd4184b561ea747be652fc3dee7fc5e1c5103f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. We clearly want the intersection point. So we're trying to solve the system of equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dd4184b561ea747be652fc3dee7fc5e1c5103f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b7bd588dade0077e6ae1a9be7c4b7d55b9b30a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)^2+y^2=2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d498e47847431c98fc06a9b684db142c1c62bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/90695790cf4dc2368b85771e0899f67e6bac53f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, our desired answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6712c172857fd1302266e65ce5918a4cc220e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arcsin{\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}}}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"46\" /> (the angle we want divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />). Since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af02f4e340401c9012a076517e5d7eaa689cf06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\arcsin{\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}}=\\arccos{\\frac{7}{8}}=\\arccos{(1-2 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})^{2})}=2\\arcsin{\\frac{1}{4}}\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>where the last step holds by the double angle formula, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effb1367acb9cfe4cf216bcf295fb41440699251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(E)\\frac{2\\arcsin{\\frac{1}{4}}}{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"53\" />.\n~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_-_Law_of_Cosines_and_Double_Angle_Formula\">Solution 4 - Law of Cosines and Double Angle Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 - Law of Cosines and Double Angle Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be Cyrus's starting point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the first point he jumps to (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/7676bb86e9162142043f19c0502c5bf05e69f5dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the second point he jumps to (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd4a05effdcd1ddc8b41af4f6f0bfe820ed4d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />). Let angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5769bd8c4884b0688e98d67f254a7e3e2fa9f11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. The probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197640c1e8629a749f1cf257ff5228093fc32f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> would therefore be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331b9c7bb11fa554a4fb5577060ec2954ff2031a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2k}{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"39\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> could be on either side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> so there are two possible areas of having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197640c1e8629a749f1cf257ff5228093fc32f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />) which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffadc780e003fb48d76a323fb7dae79a3b3850b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"39\" />. Converting to radians gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/40907992ff45ac4b0a82da9f274118ff46d6e1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"39\" />. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we use the law of cosines.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e4905bdfc7849805fb2507dd52a2eddb6a191ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2 - 2 \\cdot AB \\cdot BC \\cdot \\cos k\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/7904b26efa5b5038e4f4c88de20aba74d0651576.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^2 = 2^2 + 2^2 - 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\cos k\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1afa2201ee51a508aa68c6b35b6ddb0b8c63234f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = 4 + 4 - 8 \\cos k\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/1/071329380753dceeac7bf17d610791dea26e25a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8 \\cos k = 7\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b098cf21379f42e1c0f82250cf4802f7fca4c924.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos k = \\frac{7}{8}\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cfa55aa41aa6bc92c77d2eab04529367925d02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right) = \\arcsin\\left(\\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)^2}\\right) = \\arcsin\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}}\\right) = \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{4}}\\right) = \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"831\" height=\"64\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80ce4b364c5558ed51c5191eb0e21379b331806.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\arcsin\\left(\\sin\\left(\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\right) \\cos\\left(\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\right)\\right) = \\arcsin\\left(\\sin\\left(2 \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\right)\\right) = 2 \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\]\" width=\"754\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c82c7a45aa9d877a7cabea6a19b9ed19aed4bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k}{\\pi} = \\frac{2 \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}{\\pi}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_-_Complex_Number_and_Double_Angle_Formula\">Solution 5 - Complex Number and Double Angle Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 - Complex Number and Double Angle Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_amc_12_A_p20.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ad/2023_amc_12_A_p20.png/400px-2023_amc_12_A_p20.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"408\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ad/2023_amc_12_A_p20.png/600px-2023_amc_12_A_p20.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ad/2023_amc_12_A_p20.png/800px-2023_amc_12_A_p20.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption> </figcaption></figure>\n<p>The frog jumps 2 units in one direction, which we can represent as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8e07cc29fe69fe9b20d0fcb79264896977b9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = 2e^{ia}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the angle in radians. Then, the frog jumps another 2 units in a different direction, represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee057567ecdbf6a9a94f1993a49c4fe4d77324d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 = 2e^{ib}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle in radians.\n</p><p>The total displacement from the starting position is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36af1c7ef90312c63279cd3225ca9bf814b473e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 = z_1 + z_2 = 2e^{ia} + 2e^{ib}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe need to find the condition under which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be04f5459c3e58821642857450f43df02251836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z_3| &lt;= 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. This translates to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/1993753ace0a271581ad6682a6e09aeb9752ef1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|2e^{ia} + 2e^{ib}| &lt;= 1\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974db9d1b14997ffd17d4e9c5413b762ad2eeed8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|e^{ia} + e^{ib}| &lt;= \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e8c54800ee1cbc60a91072376771bf57581820.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e^{ia} + e^{ib} = \\cos(a) + i\\sin(a) + \\cos(b) + i\\sin(b)\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2b018009321b1252fa1368b4d62a6d5a2df2cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (\\cos(a) + \\cos(b)) + i(\\sin(a) + \\sin(b))\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The magnitude squared of this sum is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b543ee2463ec5e1491380404c459cc0eaf7af0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|e^{ia} + e^{ib}|^2 = (\\cos(a) + \\cos(b))^2 + (\\sin(a) + \\sin(b))^2\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3c493029d7f16a5c77fca0c0655646e56aeca8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\cos^2(a) + 2\\cos(a)\\cos(b) + \\cos^2(b) + \\sin^2(a) + 2\\sin(a)\\sin(b) + \\sin^2(b)\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/184cfb0a44d32645f7c92c9dd3423b9bf6962ec8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2 + 2(\\cos(a)\\cos(b) + \\sin(a)\\sin(b))\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9fa4178ee1ebf7f3d0b276cb98a74a655fc60f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2 + 2\\cos(a - b)\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ee8d8249db43d58209679d206b10363e78ee09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 + 2\\cos(a - b) &lt;= \\frac{1}{4}\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b01c91f6d307a147336447cde10fea1ee1361de1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cos(a - b) &lt;= -\\frac{7}{4}\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92bfbbea6fc04757bc2b874af0aa2b5f0af1d3e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(a - b) &lt;= -\\frac{7}{8}\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, our desired answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/55747beb3b636e445cfa5230d26a56be4f8cd08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arccos{\\frac{7}{8}}}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"42\" /> (the angle we want divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />). Since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae0876bd981790a1bc9387a16bc907a5bfb60f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\arccos{\\frac{7}{8}}=\\arccos{(1-2 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})^{2})}=2\\arcsin{\\frac{1}{4}}\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>where the last step holds by the double angle formula, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effb1367acb9cfe4cf216bcf295fb41440699251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(E)\\frac{2\\arcsin{\\frac{1}{4}}}{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hBf_SVKK9tE\">https://youtu.be/hBf_SVKK9tE</a> \n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nGZ9goJmg4Q\">https://youtu.be/nGZ9goJmg4Q</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_i_d-C1cjyI\">https://youtu.be/_i_d-C1cjyI</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B\">2023 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title